      "side": 0,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what\u0027s wrong with using this `iommu-\u003eagaw` which, AFAICS, is correctly calculated per IOMMU before deprivileging.\n\nWhat exactly is the problem? Looking at the analysis in b/517581134:\n\n\u003e ...when host names different units for the two hypercalls and the units have different agaw, the invariant breaks with no check in between.\n\nSo, sounds like _that_ is the problem we should fix? i.e. we shouldn\u0027t allow the host to \"name\" a different IOMMU than the one the domain was created for?",
      "revId": "e9b7ac9f27e73f9da0f1e544eed112afed3647d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
